
Cheat Sheet for Domain 4

ENCRYPTION:
├── At rest: SSE-S3, SSE-KMS, SSE-C, Redshift encryption
├── In transit: TLS/HTTPS, SSL connections, VPN/IPSec
├── Company manages keys: KMS CMK
├── Keys NEVER leave HSM: CloudHSM
└── Auto-rotation: KMS CMK supports annual auto-rotation

VPC NETWORKING (NO INTERNET requirement):
├── Need S3 access         → VPC Gateway Endpoint (free)
├── Need DynamoDB access   → VPC Gateway Endpoint (free)
├── Need Glue/KMS/STS etc. → VPC Interface Endpoint (PrivateLink)
├── NAT Gateway            → PROVIDES internet (violates "no internet")
└── Gateway Endpoint       → NO internet, traffic stays in AWS

LAKE FORMATION:
├── Overrides IAM (doesn't delete policies)
├── Must disable "Use only IAM access control"
├── Audit logs → WHO accessed WHICH table/column WHEN
├── Best practice: IAM + Lake Formation together (defense-in-depth)
└── Row/Column/Tag security all stack together

AUDITING:
├── Table-level access audit    → Lake Formation audit logs
├── API call audit              → CloudTrail
├── S3 object access            → S3 access logs or CloudTrail data events
└── Query performance           → CloudWatch Logs

1. CloudHSM vs KMS:
   ├── "FIPS 140-2 Level 3" → CloudHSM
   ├── "Exclusive control of HSM" → CloudHSM
   ├── "Company manages keys" (no HSM mention) → KMS CMK
   └── KMS = shared multi-tenant; CloudHSM = dedicated single-tenant

2. VPC GATEWAY ENDPOINTS (only 2 exist!):
   ├── S3 → Gateway Endpoint (free)
   ├── DynamoDB → Gateway Endpoint (free)
   └── EVERYTHING ELSE → Interface Endpoint (PrivateLink, paid)
       (Glue, KMS, CloudWatch, STS, Secrets Manager, etc.)

3. Lake Formation GetDataAccess:
   ├── LF grant on table (SELECT) → needed
   ├── IAM: lakeformation:GetDataAccess → ALSO needed
   └── Missing either = "Access Denied"

4. KMS Key Rotation:
   ├── Old data stays encrypted with OLD key material
   ├── KMS retains ALL old key versions (never deletes)
   ├── New data uses new key material
   └── NO automatic re-encryption of existing data

  24. AWS Config (Compliance Monitoring)

WHAT: Continuously monitors AWS resource configurations for compliance
HOW: Records configuration changes + evaluates against rules

KEY CONCEPTS:
├── Configuration Recorder: Tracks all resource config changes
├── Config Rules: Define desired state (managed or custom)
│   ├── Managed rules: Pre-built (e.g., s3-bucket-encryption-enabled)
│   ├── Custom rules: Lambda function evaluates compliance
│   └── Triggers: On config change OR periodic (every 1/3/6/12/24 hours)
├── Compliance Dashboard: Shows compliant vs non-compliant resources
├── Remediation: Auto-fix non-compliant resources (SSM Automation)
└── Configuration Timeline: History of all changes to a resource

DATA ENGINEERING USE CASES:
├── "S3 buckets must have encryption enabled" → Config rule
├── "Redshift clusters must have encryption" → Config rule
├── "All Glue jobs must have security configuration" → Config rule
├── "DynamoDB tables must have encryption" → Config rule
├── "Detect unencrypted resources" → Config compliance check
└── "Auto-remediate: enable encryption if missing" → Config + SSM Automation

AWS CONFIG vs CLOUDTRAIL:
├── CloudTrail: WHO did WHAT (API calls, user actions)
├── Config: WHAT is the current STATE of resources (configuration)
├── CloudTrail: "Who deleted the S3 bucket?"
├── Config: "Is the S3 bucket encrypted? Was it always encrypted?"
└── Both complement each other for full governance

EXAM TRIGGER:
├── "Ensure all S3 buckets are encrypted" → AWS Config rule
├── "Detect non-compliant resources" → AWS Config
├── "Auto-remediate security violations" → Config + SSM Automation
├── "Configuration change history" → AWS Config timeline
├── "Who made the change?" → CloudTrail (not Config)
└── "What is the current state?" → AWS Config (not CloudTrail)

25. Service Control Policies (SCPs)

WHAT: Organization-level policies that set MAXIMUM permissions
WHERE: Applied to AWS Organization OUs (Organizational Units) or accounts
WHO: Affects ALL users/roles in the target accounts (even root!)

KEY FACTS:
├── SCPs DON'T grant permissions — they set boundaries
├── SCP + IAM: Effective permission = intersection of both
├── Even if IAM allows it, SCP can DENY it
├── Applied at OU level → affects all accounts in that OU
└── Root account of member accounts IS affected by SCPs

DATA ENGINEERING USE CASES:
├── "Prevent creating resources outside eu-west-1" (data residency)
│   └── SCP: Deny all actions where region ≠ eu-west-1
├── "Prevent disabling CloudTrail" (audit protection)
│   └── SCP: Deny cloudtrail:StopLogging
├── "Prevent deleting S3 buckets in production"
│   └── SCP: Deny s3:DeleteBucket in prod OU
├── "Restrict which KMS keys can be used"
│   └── SCP: Deny kms:CreateKey unless specific conditions
└── "Prevent leaving the organization"
    └── SCP: Deny organizations:LeaveOrganization

SCP vs IAM POLICY vs LAKE FORMATION:
├── SCP: Guardrails at organization level (what's POSSIBLE)
├── IAM: Permissions at user/role level (what's ALLOWED)
├── Lake Formation: Data-level permissions (what DATA is accessible)
└── All three can coexist — most restrictive wins

EXAM TRIGGER:
├── "Prevent resources outside specific region" → SCP
├── "Organization-wide security guardrail" → SCP
├── "Even admin cannot bypass" → SCP (affects all, including admins)
├── "Data residency enforcement" → SCP (region restriction)
└── "Individual user permissions" → IAM (not SCP)

26. AWS RAM (Resource Access Manager)

WHAT: Share AWS resources across accounts without duplication
USED WITH: Lake Formation, Redshift, RAM-compatible resources

LAKE FORMATION + RAM (Cross-Account Sharing):
├── Step 1: Account A (producer) grants LF permissions to Account B
├── Step 2: LF uses RAM to share the Glue Catalog resource
├── Step 3: Account B creates a RESOURCE LINK to the shared table
├── Step 4: Account B users query via the resource link
└── Data stays in Account A's S3 — no copying!

RESOURCE LINK:
├── A pointer in Account B's Glue Catalog → Account A's table
├── Account B queries the resource link (not the original table directly)
├── Permissions still controlled by Lake Formation
└── Think: "shortcut" or "symbolic link" to shared resource

WHAT CAN BE SHARED VIA RAM:
├── Glue Data Catalog databases/tables (via Lake Formation)
├── Redshift datashares
├── VPC subnets
├── Transit Gateway
├── Route 53 Resolver rules
└── License Manager configurations

EXAM TRIGGER:
├── "Share Lake Formation tables cross-account" → LF grant + RAM + resource link
├── "Query another account's data without copying" → RAM sharing
├── "Resource link" in answer → cross-account LF sharing pattern
├── "Share Glue Catalog across accounts" → RAM
└── "Cross-account Redshift" → Redshift Data Sharing (not RAM)

27. Glue Connection Properties

WHAT: Configuration for Glue to connect to external data stores
TYPES: JDBC, MongoDB, Kafka, Network (for VPC resources)

JDBC CONNECTION:
├── JDBC URL: jdbc:mysql://hostname:3306/database
├── Username/Password (or Secrets Manager reference)
├── VPC, Subnet, Security Group (for VPC-based databases)
├── SSL: Require SSL for encrypted connections
└── Availability Zone: Must match the database's AZ

COMMON ISSUES:
├── "Connection failed" → Security group doesn't allow Glue's SG inbound
├── "SSL handshake failed" → Certificate not trusted / SSL not configured
├── "Timeout" → Wrong VPC/subnet, or database not reachable
├── "Authentication failed" → Wrong credentials or expired password
└── "No route to host" → Missing VPC endpoint or NAT for external DB

NETWORK CONNECTION (VPC):
├── Required when Glue job needs to access VPC resources
├── Specifies: VPC, Subnet, Security Group
├── Glue creates ENIs in your subnet (needs available IPs!)
├── If subnet runs out of IPs → connection fails
└── Security group must allow outbound to target (port 3306/5432/5439)

EXAM TRIGGER:
├── "Glue can't connect to RDS" → Check security group + VPC connection
├── "Glue job in VPC needs S3" → VPC endpoint (not connection property)
├── "Encrypt JDBC connection" → Enable SSL in connection properties
├── "Glue connection timeout" → Network misconfiguration (SG/subnet/VPC)
└── "Rotate database password for Glue" → Secrets Manager + update connection
